        "text": "Security update for python-cryptography",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for python-cryptography fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-69247: PKCS#7 `EnvelopedData` decryption exposes a Bleichenbacher oracle through distinguishable errors and\n  timing (bsc#1273551).\n- CVE-2026-69248: verifier accepts wildcard DNS names allowing escape from `permittedSubtrees` (bsc#1273549).\n- CVE-2026-69249: duplicate self-signed intermediates can cause exponential path-building (bsc#1273516).\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
